00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
Canadian investors holding TSX positions after yesterday's record close should watch how easing Middle East tensions reshape sector leadership into next week. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 128. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:52.640
putting real money to work. The S and P500 closed at 7,737. That marks a gain of 1.8%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,585. The TSX composite closed at 35,802. Tech and mining shares led the TSX advance.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:01:10.120
Broader sentiment stayed supported by cooling geopolitical headlines. The nearest Fed decision remains the September meeting. Markets are pricing a possible hold or modest tightening bias after Kansas City Fed President Schmid called current policy insufficiently restrictive.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:24.080
Earning season continues with AMD's just reported results providing a fresh data point on AI infrastructure demand. Remember, we covered DAL about 26 days ago on an earning surprise entry.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:35.900
The lesson there was that even strong fundamentals can be overwhelmed by sector rotation. Buying calls instead of shares lets investors control the same number of shares with far less capital.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:49.140
This approach accepts a defined break even point above the strike. Today's environment of elevated equity prices makes this capital efficiency trade off, especially relevant for TFSA accounts.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:02:10.020
Those accounts face strict contribution limits. An investor comparing a $100 stock purchase to a $5 call option can see the call requires roughly 5% of the cash outlay. Yet the call still delivers similar upside above its break even. The approach has historically performed best in moderately bullish markets.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:28.320
Volatility keeps option premiums reasonable in those conditions. The main risk is time decay if the move does not materialize quickly. Platforms such as quest trade or interactive brokers display side-by-side capital and break even calculations directly in the options chain.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:39.120
The same comparison also shows that the call buyer's maximum loss stays limited to the premium paid. Share ownership carries full downside exposure to zero.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:50.680
This structure becomes particularly useful when an investor already holds a concentrated position. The investor wants to add exposure without committing additional TFSA room.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:03:06.700
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. The pick is AMD on the NASDAQ. The sector is tech. The strategy is post earnings positioning ahead of potential follow-through in AI-related names.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:23.020
The hold period runs Monday through Friday. The catalyst is quarterly results just released. Market attention focuses on data center and AI revenue trends. Price action following the print will be measured against the 20-day and 50-day moving averages.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:43.600
Volume above the 20-day average on any rebound would strengthen the setup. A failure to hold the post earnings low could trigger a 4-6% retracement. The stop loss sits 6% below entry. The target ranges from 3% to 7% over the 5-day window if sector rotation remains supportive.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:52.260
Confidence sits at medium because the earnings catalyst is present with sector momentum. No volume confirmation is yet available.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:04:01.860
This trade demonstrates how to size an entry immediately after an earnings release. It still requires volume confirmation before treating the move as confirmed.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:11.020
Listeners learn to separate the headline reaction from the subsequent price action that actually determines whether the catalyst produces excess return.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:27.520
The same process highlights why a single earnings print must still clear the volume filter before capital is committed. The options play growth lab overlays capital requirements, break even prices and probability of profit metrics directly on the options chain.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:39.780
Users can compare share ownership versus call buying in real time. It gives retail investors the same side-by-side analysis previously available only to institutional desks.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:54.160
Canadian users can access it through a standard brokerage login without additional fees for the basic comparison view. The tool surfaces the exact dollar difference in capital outlay and the precise break even price for each strike.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:01.640
This feature set proves especially useful inside contribution limited accounts where every dollar of buying power matters.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:09.680
Research estimates roughly $36 trillion will move to Gen 10 and Millennial households over the next 20 years.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:21.640
Down payment assistance already appears in 2025 survey data. The scale implies sustained demand for broad equity exposure as recipients deploy capital into long-term holdings.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:34.580
Seasonally adjusted annual home sales reached approximately 4.4 million. That level sits up 4.2% year over year. The reading marks the highest since November 2022.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:43.580
Starlink and AI businesses drove nearly double revenue and narrower operating losses in SpaceX's first public earnings release.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:53.520
Sales per subscriber declined even as total revenue climbed. That points to a shift toward lower ARPU enterprise and government contracts.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:06:09.160
A 2025 true work survey showed more than half of recent buyers counted on lower rates to ease budgets. The finding underscores why rate decisions continue to influence both housing related equities and consumer discretionary names.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:19.180
Total trades stand at 43. The win rate sits at 54% that breaks down to 23 wins, 19 losses and 1 break even.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:32.020
